eria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Treat the pinned Pandoc-version-to-output coupling as an explicit external boundary. Any accepted golden fixture must identify its Pandoc version and provide a documented regeneration command.'","test_wiki_render_corpus.py:73-88 keys the shared render on a live `_pandoc_stamp()` (version|path|size); the wiki extra pins `pypandoc-binary==1.15` precisely because pandoc's jira writer changes escaping between releases — freezing to a static fixture drops the live version check from the per-change path.","ABSENCE: the plan requires identifying the version and a regen command, but not a mechanism (e.g. a CI assertion that the fixture stamp equals the installed pandoc version, or a scheduled off-hot-path full-corpus re-run) that FIRES the regen when the pin moves."],"finding":"The golden-fixture Pandoc proposal specifies a version stamp and a regeneration command but names no trigger that revalidates the fixture when the pinned Pandoc version actually changes, so a dependency bump could leave the frozen fixture asserting stale bytes against a newer binary that the hot path no longer exercises.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff1c507b9df7880a2","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullet 2 (Pandoc/render_unit) and AC lines 'Every accepted golden fixture identifies the exact Pandoc version' / 'includes a documented runnable regeneration command'","norm_id":"n0cea19647b1f07ef","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future PR bumps pypandoc-binary; the golden fixtures still assert 1.15-era bytes and pass, while real DC output changes silently.","The pinned pandoc binary is rebuilt/repackaged at the same version string but different escaping; the static fixture never detects it."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add to the Pandoc lever a fixture-vs-binary drift guard: a fast test asserting the golden fix